 called mash I wrote  this myself I really don't know I just  don't know his name when Dylan went in  to meet on the roll he was so nervous he  was practically shaking he was so  worried he wasn't going to get the part  he sits down to meet Ingo and he goes  says you were really great in that movie  and the Dirty Dozen and Donald's exhales  with relief and then Ingo pauses and  says well it could have been the  director his son rogue shared a story  with me when shooting the dry white  season he uprooted the family to  Zimbabwe  Donald was up early as always to shower  and the phone rang  rogue answered and the ad told him that  Donald wasn't needed at work that day  because mr. Brando wasn't able to shoot  that day  rogue passed along the message to his  dad who said until I can do that myself  I am nothing well at 82 years old he has  never missed a call time he is always  the first one to set and has famously  rewritten the dialog of all of his  scenes before the director has even  arrived on set much to their dismay he  is honestly and truly something else  which is why I am so proud to be here if  we had an honor a knighthood I think  he'd be Sir Donald Sir Sutherland that  is an honor to present this overdue  Oscar to a great magician a phenomenal  actor a wonderful role model and a  terrific human being with an enviable an  impressive body of work the great Donald  Sutherland  [Applause]
 

